.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 10, 2026
.Dt DTFL_STRERROR 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_strerror ,
.Nm dtfl_last_error_detail ,
.Nm dtfl_version
.Nd libdtfl error reporting and version
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libdtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/base.h
.Ft const char *
.Fn dtfl_strerror "int err"
.Ft const char *
.Fn dtfl_last_error_detail "void"
.Ft const char *
.Fn dtfl_version "void"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Fallible libdtfl functions return 0 on success or a
.Dv DTFL_E*
code.
.Fn dtfl_strerror
returns a static description of a code.
.Fn dtfl_last_error_detail
returns a description of the most recent error on the calling thread,
including the values involved, or the empty string.
The string remains valid until the calling thread's next libdtfl call.
.Fn dtfl_version
returns the library version string.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
All three return non-NULL strings that the caller must not free.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width DTFL_EALGEBRA
.It Dv DTFL_EINVAL
Invalid argument.
.It Dv DTFL_ENOMEM
Allocation failed, from functions documented as reporting it.
.It Dv DTFL_ERANGE
A value is outside a representable range.
.It Dv DTFL_ESTATE
The operation is not valid in the current state.
.It Dv DTFL_EALGEBRA
A diff class lacks an operation that an operator needs.
.It Dv DTFL_EIO
An I/O or network operation failed.
.It Dv DTFL_EPROTO
Wire data is malformed.
.It Dv DTFL_ENOTSUP
The feature is not supported in this build.
.It Dv DTFL_EOF
End of stream.
.El
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
All three may be called from any thread.
The detail buffer is per thread.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
int rc = dtfl_execute(&cfg, worker_main, NULL, &guards);
if (rc != 0)
	errx(1, "%s: %s", dtfl_strerror(rc), dtfl_last_error_detail());
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
These replace Rust's
.Vt Result
error values.
